{{!
    @template block_socialcomments/post

    A comment or a reply: picture and name of the author, the date and the text.

    Context variables required for this template:
    * fullname - Name of the author
    * time - The date as shown, e.g. "5 minutes ago"
    * exacttime - The exact date and time, for the tooltip
    * datetime - The date in ISO 8601 format
    * content - The formatted text (HTML)

    Optional context variables:
    * userpicture - Picture of the author (HTML)
    * groupname - The group the comment was posted to (formatted)
    * raw - The text as written, for editing it
    * actions - Menu to edit or delete the post (HTML)

    Example context (json):
    {
        "fullname": "Amelia Clarke",
        "userpicture": "<span class=\"userinitials size-35\">AC</span>",
        "time": "5 minutes ago",
        "exacttime": "29 October 2026, 02:05 PM",
        "datetime": "2026-10-29T14:05:00+01:00",
        "content": "Can someone explain why a smaller f-number means a bigger aperture?",
        "groupname": "Team North",
        "raw": "Can someone explain why a smaller f-number means a bigger aperture?",
        "actions": ""
    }
}}
<div class="sc-post">
    {{#userpicture}}<div class="sc-post-picture">{{{userpicture}}}</div>{{/userpicture}}
    <div class="sc-post-main">
        <div class="sc-post-header">
            <span class="sc-post-author">{{fullname}}</span>
            <time class="sc-post-time" datetime="{{datetime}}" title="{{exacttime}}">{{time}}</time>
            {{#groupname}}<span class="sc-post-group">{{{groupname}}}</span>{{/groupname}}
            {{#actions}}<div class="sc-post-menu">{{{actions}}}</div>{{/actions}}
        </div>
        <div class="sc-post-content" data-region="content"{{#raw}} data-raw="{{raw}}"{{/raw}}>{{{content}}}</div>
    </div>
</div>
